# The printer hook in the firmware: [F]irmware installs it (the user
# firmware's message), TOS goes on to run PRPATHS from the floppy's AUTO
# folder, and its four print paths and the screen dump go into the hook's RAM
# buffer instead of the printer port (Hatari's printer port gets nothing);
# then the desktop.
@printer
@disk-a tools/dev/builds/disks/prpaths.st
text "Atari +: (ST|STE|Mega STE), TOS" 1500
key f
key 0x1c
wait 100
key 0x01
wait 900
shot prpaths
key 0x39
wait 150
key 0x39
wait 150
key 0x39
wait 150
key 0x39
wait 150
key 0x39
wait 300
shot done
hookstate
# PRPATHS ends on a key, and TOS goes on to its desktop
key 0x39
desktop 2500
